# Build context for every service image.
#
# Each Dockerfile does a single `COPY . .`, so this file — not a
# hand-maintained list of module paths inside seven Dockerfiles — decides
# what the build sees. Adding a Maven module therefore needs no Dockerfile
# change, which is what broke the build when automarket-messaging was added.
#
# Anything the Maven build needs (pom.xml, */pom.xml, */src) must stay.

# ── VCS, IDE, agent config ───────────────────────────────────────
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github
.idea
.vscode
.claude
claude-prompts
*.iml

# ── Build output — stale classes must not shadow a fresh build ───
**/target

# ── Secrets and local state ──────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.local
uploads
k8s/secret.yml

# ── Deployment, docs, fixtures — not build inputs ────────────────
k8s
docker-compose.yml
Dockerfile
**/Dockerfile
*.md
*.pdf
prometheus.yml
grafana-datasources.yml
seed.sql
mock_data
